# Master Knowledge Index — Cross-references all topics across all domains
# Updated by kb-topic-expander after each /learn session.
# Updated by kb-index-rebuild if run manually.
#
# PURPOSE: Single source of truth for what's in the knowledge base. Agents
# consult this before fetching article content so they know what exists and
# whether it's current for your expertise level.
#
# STRUCTURE:
#   topics[]         — flat list of all articles across all domains
#   domain_summaries — per-domain stats for quick overview
#   stubs[]          — topics encountered but not yet written
#   last_rebuilt     — ISO 8601 datetime of last full index rebuild
#
# NOTE: Per-domain indexes (knowledge/{domain}/_index.yaml) follow the same
# format but scoped to that domain. The master index aggregates them all.
#
# STATUS VALUES:
#   complete  — full article written at your current expertise level
#   stub      — title + frontmatter created, content not yet written
#   outdated  — article exists but your expertise level has changed since writing
#   draft     — work in progress

